        {
          "type": "definition",
          "term": "Time complexity",
          "content": "How the **number of steps** (and so the running time) of an algorithm **grows as the size of the input *n* grows**. It is usually described for the **worst case** using **Big O notation**."
        },
        {
          "type": "comparison",
