        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "pseudocode",
          "content": "count ← 0\nFOR i ← 1 TO n\n    FOR j ← 1 TO n\n        count ← count + 1      // runs n × n times\n    NEXT j\nNEXT i",
          "caption": "Counting the steps of nested loops — O(n²)"
        },
        {
          "type": "exam_tip",
          "content": "To find the complexity, look at the **loops**: one loop over the data → O(n); two nested loops → O(n²); halving the data each step → O(log n). Ignore constants: 3n + 5 is O(n)."
        }
      ]
